# The patching-hosts skill's host knob (#192). Grammar: the vendored skill's
# references/knob.md. The skill reads this file and never writes it; a
# malformed line makes the host report-only (tests/test_patching_hosts_knob.py).
#
# Times are UTC. Every range covers both Pacific offsets (PDT UTC-7, PST UTC-8),
# so nothing needs revisiting at a DST change.
class production
posture scheduled

window Tue 15:15-23:30             # 08:15-16:30 PDT / 07:15-15:30 PST

# Ingest timers (infra/*.timer): each has RandomizedDelaySec=300. A scrape task
# ran 5m43s on 2026-10-06; a refresh can take ~20 min.
quiet 07:25-09:05                  # 00:30 PT scrape
quiet 13:25-15:05                  # 06:30 PT scrape
quiet 08:55-11:35 Sun              # 02:00 PT address backfill, 03:00 PT disk hygiene

# wslcb-task@ is Type=oneshot: a running task is "activating", not "active".
inflight systemctl list-units 'wslcb-task@*' --state=activating,active,deactivating --no-legend | wc -l
service wslcb-web.service
restarter wslcb-healthcheck.timer
health curl -sf http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health

# wslcb_test is the pytest database (TEST_DATABASE_URL).
datastore postgres postgresql@16-main wslcb wslcb_test

# The nightly GCS backup (#185, docs/RECOVERY.md) stands in for the recovery
# point's own dump of this cluster. It dumps wslcb only, so wslcb_test (pytest
# scratch, rebuilt by alembic upgrade head) gets no dump (#220).
backup wslcb-backup.service postgresql@16-main

# Third-party apt origins, maintenance lane (#220). Tailscale was installed
# 2026-10-09; its own auto-update is off (AutoUpdate.Apply false), so apt is
# its only path. Scoped by pins in /etc/apt/preferences.d/tailscale (policy.md
# "Two lanes"). Its own held step: the tailscaled restart drops MagicDNS for a
# few seconds, and the co-status check-ins reach http://status:9000 over the
# tailnet, so that drop is approved on its own.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale

# fwupd (the image ships it, masks its units and deletes its motd conffile, so
# unattended-upgrade skipped it and exited 1) was purged with its 53 orphaned
# dependencies on 2026-10-08 (#193). The masks stay. Savepoint, kept until the
# review: /var/backups/patching-hosts-prune-fwupd. Review: does the base image
# still ship it?
exception purged:fwupd 2027-04-08 purged with its orphans; the image still ships it, masked, and its deleted motd conffile would block unattended-upgrade if fwupd were reinstalled (#193)
